From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: prime QCA8386 switch id before MDIO probe

QCA8386 uses the MHT register-address encoding in qca8k_read_mii() and
qca8k_write_mii().  Those helpers currently select that encoding from
priv->switch_id, but qca8k_read_switch_id() only assigns switch_id after
the first register read has succeeded.  Consequently the initial mask
control read for QCA8386 is issued with the legacy qca8k encoding.

Prime switch_id from the compatible's match data for QCA8386 before the
validation read.  qca8k_read_switch_id() still reads the hardware ID,
checks it against the match data, and assigns the detected value, so the
device validation is not weakened.  Leave all older qca8k variants on
their existing probe path.

---
 drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -2275,6 +2275,14 @@ static int qca8k_sw_probe(struct mdio_device *mdiodev)
 	}
 
 	priv->mdio_cache.page = 0xffff;
+
+	/* QCA8386 needs MHT addressing for the very first register read.
+	 * The hardware ID is still read and validated below.
+	 */
+	if (priv->info && priv->info->id == QCA8K_ID_QCA8386) {
+		priv->switch_id = priv->info->id;
+		dev_info(priv->dev, "using QCA8386 MHT addressing for ID probe\n");
+	}
 
 	/* Check the detected switch id */
 	ret = qca8k_read_switch_id(priv);
-- 
2.50.1
